#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:5
msgid "Model zoo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:7
msgid ""
"Community- and partner-contributed PyBaMM models. Each entry is one self-"
"contained folder with its own maintainer, tests, examples, and citation; the "
"table below is generated from those folders' manifests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:11
msgid ""
"The zoo is a separate distribution, released independently of PyBaMM, so "
"`pip install pybamm` does not provide it. Install it from [PyPI](https://"
"pypi.org/project/pybamm-model-zoo/):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:15
msgid "pip install pybamm-model-zoo\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:19
msgid ""
"A model with third-party dependencies of its own declares them as an extra "
"named `zoo-<slug>`, and the `zoo-all` extra installs every model's:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:22
msgid "pip install \"pybamm-model-zoo[zoo-all]\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:26
msgid ""
"Zoo models are then reached through the zoo's registry, not the `pybamm` "
"namespace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:29
msgid ""
"import pybamm\n"
"import pybamm_model_zoo as zoo\n"
"\n"
"model = zoo.load(zoo.list_models()[0])()\n"
"solution = pybamm.Simulation(model).solve([0, 3600])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/index.md:37
msgid ""
"Models in the **core** tier are covered by PyBaMM's merge gate. Models in "
"the **community** tier are tested on every pull request too, but their "
"results are advisory: a red community model never blocks a PyBaMM merge. See "
"[contributing a model](contributing.md) to add your own."
msgstr ""

